# Workspace Context — INENI-PT-GROUP-B

This is the local workspace for the INENI-PT-GROUP-B platform engineering
project. Repositories are cloned here as siblings: `platform/`,
`platform-iac/`, `platform-gitops/`, `app-backend/`, `app-frontend/`,
`.github/`.

## Mandatory session bootstrap

**Before responding to the user's first project-related question, read
these files in order. Do not answer based on memory alone — always read
the current files first:**

1. `platform/docs/claude/project-overview.md`
2. `platform/docs/claude/architecture-decisions.md`
3. `platform/docs/claude/repository-layout.md`
4. `platform/docs/claude/conventions.md`
5. `platform/docs/claude/working-with-claude.md`
6. `platform/CONTRIBUTING.md`

These files contain the project's hard constraints, tool decisions,
repository topology, commit/PR rules, and AI usage policy. They override
any prior assumption.

Read `platform/docs/claude/tooling-reference.md` additionally when the
question concerns Kubernetes manifests, Terraform, Crossplane, ESO,
ExternalDNS, cert-manager, CloudNativePG, or Prometheus/Grafana.

## Language rules — strict

These rules apply unconditionally and override any user-level preference
for INENI-PT-GROUP-B work:

- **All artefacts are written in English.** This includes code, code
  comments, commit messages, branch names, file names, variable names,
  pull request titles and descriptions, issue titles and descriptions,
  release notes, and all committed documentation.
- **Conversation language in the chat window is the user's choice.** It
  is configured in the user-level memory (`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` on
  Linux/WSL, `%USERPROFILE%\.claude\CLAUDE.md` on Windows). Respect that
  setting for the conversational wrapper around your output.
- **Mixed-language artefacts are not allowed.** A commit message in
  German with English code is wrong. A PR description in German is wrong.
  An issue body in German is wrong. The user's conversation language has
  no influence on the artefact language.

## Other precedence

If anything in this workspace's context conflicts with the user-level
memory at `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (Linux/WSL) or
`%USERPROFILE%\.claude\CLAUDE.md` (Windows), the project context wins
for INENI-PT-GROUP-B work. The project files at
`platform/docs/claude/*.md` and `platform/CONTRIBUTING.md` are the
binding source of truth.

## How this file is maintained

The canonical version of this file lives at
`platform/docs/setup/workspace-CLAUDE.md.template` in the `platform`
repository. It is copied by each team member into their local workspace
root and is not itself committed (the workspace root is not a git repo).

If you change this file locally, consider whether the change should flow
back to the template via a PR to `platform`. If yes: edit
`platform/docs/setup/workspace-CLAUDE.md.template`, open a PR, and
notify the team to re-copy after merge.
